<title>DENMARK: FORECAST-Denmark ups 1996 GDP expectations.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Denmark ups 1996 GDP expectations.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish gross domestic product (GDP) will grow by 2.0 in 1996 and 3.1 pct in 1997, after a growth rate  of 2.6 percent in 1995, the Danish Economy Ministry said in its latest economic survey issued on Monday.</p>
<p>The figures compared with a 1.8 percent growth forecast for 1996 and 3.0 percent for 1997 in its last survey in August. --Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
